\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse
\par Assembly
\par 
\par \'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, behold us with Thy blessing,
\par Once again assembled here;
\par Onward be our footsteps pressing,
\par In Thy love, and faith and fear;
\par Still protect us
\par By Thy presence ever near.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. For Thy mercy we adore Thee,
\par For this rest upon our way;
\par Lord, again we bow before Thee,
\par Speed our labours day by day;
\par Mind and spirit
\par With Thy choicest gifts array.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Keep the spell of home affection
\par Still alive in every heart;
\par May its power, with mild direction,
\par Draw our love from self apart,
\par Till Thy children
\par Feel that Thou their Father art.
\par Amen.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse
\par Dismissal
\par \cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, dismiss us with Thy blessing
\par Thanks for mercies past receive;
\par Pardon all, their faults confessing;
\par Time that is lost may all retrieve;
\par May Thy children
\par Ne'er again Thy Spirit grieve.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. By Thy kindly influence cherish
\par All the good we all hear have gained;
\par May all taint of evil perish,
\par By Thy mightier power restraine;
\par Seek we ever
\par Knowledge pure and love unfeigned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Let Thy Father-hand be shieding
\par All who here shall meet no more;
\par May their seed-time past be yielding
\par Year by year a richer store;
\par Those returning
\par Make more faithful than before.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

